{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011LTWnJYhcmEpNRdFjLKJ6h","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# The snapshot copies only what the act authorises: `copy_live` scoped to the flipped registry and the named `--approves` refs\n2\t\n3\t**Status:** plan of record for the row minted against it. Authored 2026-09-01\n4\t(evening supervised session) from the owner's question on `OI-78` — \"I would\n5\tnever expect a work lane to modify the content of the last-approved\n6\tdirectory\" — and a read-only investigation of the mechanism (an independent\n7\tOpus pass; commands quoted in the 2026-09-01 log addendum that files this).\n8\t\n9\t## 1. The problem, measured\n10\t\n11\t`baseline_snapshot.copy_live` iterates every registry in `SNAPSHOTTED` — all\n12\tseven — unconditionally (`for rel in SNAPSHOTTED: … shutil.copyfile(live,\n13\tdest)`, baseline_snapshot.py:679-696). `intake._apply_flips` is a dead arm\n14\t(OI-45 ruled (b): the action writes nothing), so `intake.py snapshot` is the\n15\tone door, and every invocation re-baselines the WHOLE tree regardless of\n16\twhich registry the approval act touched. A `Status` flip on two LLR rows\n17\ttherefore drags interfaces.toml, external.toml and components.toml along,\n18\tand any trunk-side off-spine drift present in the live files at that moment\n19\tis re-sealed as a side effect.\n20\t\n21\tThe guard did not refuse because it had nothing to refuse: `refresh_refusal`\n22\tblocks only rows whose SNAPSHOT copy claims approval and whose approved cells\n23\tmoved; every interfaces.toml row is Drafted on both sides (snapshot 135 rows,\n24\tlive 163, all Drafted), so by its own doctrine \"copying it re-blesses\n25\tnothing\". True of approval; false of the CENSUS — the only rendering of\n26\toff-spine change is computed against the snapshot, so the whole-tree copy\n27\tsilently zeroed it (132 changed / 30 added / 3 removed → 1 / 0 / 1 at the\n28\twi508 branch's `580df781`). `docs/ratify/CURRENT.md` already says this:\n29\t\"`intake.py snapshot` copies them WHOLESALE alongside any spine approval.\"\n30\t\n31\tNot a one-off: `git log -- docs/archive/last_approved` shows 9 of the 21\n32\tsnapshot commits before `580df781` (ac121647, 4fd20f89, 13593db9, 2b7be11a,\n33\t69e4a854, ad2222df, 8848f6fb, 46616726, 34a42f7e) wrote off-spine files while\n34\tonly spine `Status` moved. The wi508 handback merge and its refresh carried\n35\tthe branch bytes and nothing more (`git diff 4824c0ba..551d1b2c --\n36\tdocs/archive/last_approved/` is empty); OI-71's disposition is not causal.\n37\t\n38\tA secondary widening: `refresh_refusal` short-circuits `if approves: return\n39\t\"\"` (:536) — one `--approves` ref mutes the gate for all seven files rather\n40\tthan the registry it names.\n41\t\n42\t## 2. What this is NOT\n43\t\n44\t- Not a ruling on `OI-78`: the rows already absorbed at `580df781` stay\n45\t  absorbed until the owner rules; this plan stops the NEXT act from\n46\t  absorbing more. A byte-level restore stays unavailable (the mirror\n47\t  invariant).\n48\t- Not a change to the mirror invariant (`committed_snapshot_findings`) or to\n49\t  the seed path (`--seed` still copies everything once, on the owner's\n50\t  signing commit).\n51\t- Not a move of the snapshot write to the serial trunk lane. That is a\n52\t  legitimate alternative the owner may prefer (a lane never writes\n53\t  `docs/archive/last_approved/`; the approval act is replayed at the merge\n54\t  slot); it is recorded here as the alternative, not chosen, because it\n55\t  changes where approvals happen rather than what one approval copies, and\n56\t  the smaller change closes the class on its own. Re-open it if the owner\n57\t  rules the other way.\n58\t\n59\t## 3. Done-when\n60\t\n61\t1. `copy_live` copies ONLY the registries the act authorises: the registry\n62\t   whose `Status` flipped in the same act, plus every registry a\n63\t   `--approves` ref names — never the rest. The remaining registries' snapshot\n64\t   copies are left byte-identical to what they were (so the mirror invariant\n65\t   stays satisfied at the writing commit: an untouched file is not \"written\").\n66\t   The seed path is unchanged.\n67\t2. `--approves` becomes a NAMED list: a ref mutes `refresh_refusal` only for\n68\t   the registry it names; the other six keep their gate.\n69\t3. `intake.py snapshot`'s prose stamp records the registries the act copied\n70\t   and why (flip / named ref), so the next reader of `docs/archive/last_approved/README.md`\n71\t   sees the act's scope, not a whole-tree claim.\n72\t4. Tests in `tests/test_baseline_snapshot.py` (existing style): a spine flip\n73\t   with off-spine drift present leaves the off-spine snapshot bytes untouched\n74\t   and the census intact; a named `--approves` ref copies exactly its\n75\t   registry; the seed still copies all; the mirror invariant stays green\n76\t   across the act.\n77\t5. The queued reseal row's \"stand\" branch is re-read against the new scope:\n78\t   after this lands, that row's regeneration re-seals the four spine rows and\n79\t   nothing else, so the off-spine census survives to its own review. Its\n80\t   spec text is updated by this row (a queued spec's `## Context`/scope is\n81\t   triage, not a spine act) and the change is stated in the fragment.\n82\t6. Fragment with a file-level `Deferred open items:` line and `fig:`\n83\t   provenance on the 9-of-21 history figure (`git log --format=… --\n84\t   docs/archive/last_approved` at `6000ec9c`).\n85\t\n86\t## 4. Evidence trail\n87\t\n88\tThe 2026-09-01 log addendum that files this row; `docs/reviews/WI-568-REVIEW-A.md`\n89\trounds 4–5 and `docs/reviews/wi-555-wi508-partial-close/005-REVIEW-A-5c8a007-supervisor.md`\n90\tMAJOR 1; `docs/ratify/CURRENT.md`'s own wholesale-copy sentence; OI-45 (b);\n91\tbaseline_snapshot.py `copy_live` / `refresh_refusal` / `_record_approval`.\n92\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1f5a87ea-2697-42f1-8c89-f0f7398f