{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012phByhubtp1J7vpH47cgVm","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t+++\n2\tid = \"WI-571\"\n3\ttitle = \"The snapshot copies only what the act authorises: copy_live scoped to the flipped registry and the named --approves refs\"\n4\tworkstream = \"process\"\n5\tspecref = \"docs/plans/2026-09-01-snapshot-copy-scope.md\"\n6\tbuildtier = \"medium\"\n7\tpriority = 5\n8\tsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\n9\t+++\n10\t\n11\t## Context\n12\t\n13\tFiled 2026-09-01 (evening supervised session) from the owner's question on OI-78 and an independent investigation: baseline_snapshot.copy_live mirrors all seven registries on every intake.py snapshot act, so a spine Status flip re-seals whatever off-spine drift is live at that moment (9 of 21 prior snapshot commits did; the wi508 handback merge was not causal). Scope copy_live to the flipped registry plus the registries named by --approves; make --approves a named list; stamp the act's scope; re-read the queued reseal row's stand branch. Read the plan's section 2 before widening - moving the write to the trunk lane is the recorded alternative, not this row.\n14\t\n15\t**Standing constraint (owner ruling 2026-09-01, the approval act is the\n16\tadjudicator's):** if this row authors or amends spine rows (SR/LLR/TC), leave\n17\tthem `Drafted`; do NOT flip any `Status`, and do NOT run `intake.py snapshot`\n18\tor write `docs/archive/last_approved/` on this lane — including while testing\n19\tthe scoped copy, which must be driven on a scaffold, never on this repo's\n20\tsnapshot. The flip and the snapshot are performed on trunk by the\n21\tadjudication arm once it ships.\n22\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1f5a87ea-2697-42f1-8c89-f0f7398fc45c","uuid":"1ce7858c-9f28-4db8-a7cd-4a122b9cf9d6","timestamp":"2026-09-02T02:14:01.039Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/diytechy/Documents/ai-template-drive/wi-571-the-snapshot-copies-only-what/docs/work/active/wi-571-the-snapshot-copies-only-what/WI-571-the-snapshot-copies-only-what.md","content":"+++\nid = \"WI-571\"\ntitle = \"The snapshot copies only what the act authorises: copy_live scoped to the flipped registry and the named --approves refs\"\nworkstream = \"process\"\nspecref = \"docs/plans/2026-09-01-snapshot-copy-scope.md\"\nbuildtier = \"medium\"\npriority = 5\nsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\n+++\n\n## Context\n\nFiled 2026-09-01 (evening supervised session) from the owner's question on OI-78 and an independent investigation: baseline_snapshot.copy_live mirrors all seven registries on every intake.py snapshot act, so a spine Status flip re-seals whatever off-spine drift is live at that moment (9 of 21 prior snapshot commits did; the wi508 handback merge was not causal). Scope copy_live to the flipped registry plus the registries named by --approves; make --approves a named list; stamp the act's scope; re-read the queued reseal row's stand branch. Read the plan's section 2 before widening - moving the write to the trunk lane is the recorded alternative, not this row.\n\n**Standing constraint (owner ruling 2026-09-01, the approval act is the\nadjudicator's):** if this row authors or amends spine rows (SR/LLR/TC), leave\nthem `Drafted`; do NOT flip any `Status`, and do NOT run `intake.py snapshot`\nor write `docs/archive/last_approved/` on this lane — including while testing\nthe scoped copy, which must be driven on a scaffold, never on this repo's\nsnapshot. The flip and the snapshot are performed on trunk by the\nadjudication arm once it ships.\n","numLines":22,"startLine":1,"totalLines":22}}}
