{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CedsDZQ6kBzQQzqGs5eEJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The WI is complete and the row is closed. Final state is clean and verified.\n\n## Summary\n\n**WI-571 — the snapshot copies only what the act authorises** — shipped and closed on branch `wi-571-the-snapshot-copies-only-what`.\n\n**What changed** (`baseline_snapshot.py`, `intake.py`):\n- `copy_live` no longer re-mirrors all seven registries on a refresh. It copies **only** the registries the act authorises — every registry `--approves` names, plus every registry an approving `Status` move happened in (a flip on an existing row, or a new row arriving already `Approved`, via `_authorised_registries`) — and leaves the rest byte-identical. The seed / first-signing / unreadable-repair path still copies the whole tree (`_refresh_targets`). This closes the whole-tree re-seal that dragged live off-spine drift into the approval record on every spine-only approval.\n- `--approves` became a **named list** (`REGISTRY=REF`, `;`-joined → `{rel: ref}` via `parse_approves`/`resolve_registry`): a ref mutes `refresh_refusal` for the one registry it names, closing the `if approves: return \"\"` widening that muted all seven.\n- The prose stamp (`_record_approval`) records the act's scope per registry.\n- Both mirror rules stay green untouched because each is pinned to the file it judges — \"an untouched file is not written.\"\n\n**Verification** — driven end-to-end through the real `intake.py` CLI (scoped copy, named-ref path, unknown-registry error, per-registry refusal) plus four new scope tests and a mirror-green test. `test_baseline_snapshot` (47), `test_trace_briefs`, ratchet, complexity, and `test_intake` all green. Smoke tier within budget (21.4s/60s).\n\n**Residual failures are all pre-existing, none this WI's** — I fixed my one regression (`copy_live` C901 hit 11 → extracted `_refresh_targets`). The remaining full-suite failures are the documented ruff-0.16 `I001` scaffold-demo skew (10; `bootstrap.py` untouched) and a broken link in `docs/log.md` (WI-572's plan). The lone smoke failure — `test_wi_convert` choking on the no-frontmatter `docs/work/cancelled/README.md` — is a **pre-existing trunk defect in the drained state**, verified identical at `b8db16fd` before this WI existed; my close correctly drains the claim and unmasks it. All documented in the fragment for the trunk lane.\n\n**Close ritual complete**: Deliverable filled (before Context), `specref` cleared, no spine rows minted (no approval-brief regen owed), WI-569's `## Context` updated (triage: its regeneration now re-seals only the spine rows), spec moved to `docs/work/complete/`, final commit trailed `WI: WI-571`. Working tree clean.\n\nOne thing worth your attention: the `docs/work/cancelled/README.md` redirect stub reds the drained-state smoke bar on trunk — it wants either deletion (cancelled/ is fully archived) or a converter exclusion for status-subdir READMEs. That's its own row, not mine to fix here."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1100,"cache_read_input_tokens":283217,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1100},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1f5a87ea-2697-42f1-8c89-f0f7398fc45c","uuid":"98b557c2-d000-412a-a6db-e8eea1d55a90","request_id":"req_011CedsDXuoQNFYPCXQVbPTx"}
